<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<preface xml:id="about-this-book">
  <title>About This Book</title>

  <p>This book teaches the basics of programming. It uses JavaScript, but the ideas carry over to any language.
  It also covers the small amount of HTML and CSS you need to build a web page.</p>

  <p>The book follows the order of the Fundamentals of Software Development course.
  Each unit matches one of the course tests. A unit starts with the core chapters, which cover what the test covers.
  Optional chapters at the end of a unit go further.</p>

  <p>The book started as <pubtitle>Foundations of Python Programming</pubtitle>, a free textbook on Runestone Academy.
  Its foreword, prefaces, and contributor list are kept, unchanged, at the back of this book.</p>

  <note xml:id="notice">
    <title>Please Read</title>
    <p>This book is not made, approved, or endorsed by Operation Spark.
    It was written with help from AI and may contain mistakes.</p>
  </note>
</preface>
